{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0419"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge nature/plants","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/nature__plants.g1.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",461],["+"," Many of them must be cooked first, however: raw beans, above all the common bean (Phaseolus vulgaris), first found in Peru's Guitarrero Cave around 6000 BC, contain the toxin Phasin (phytohaemagglutinin), a lectin that clumps red blood cells and causes violent stomach upsets, and that is destroyed only by thorough boiling."],["=",630]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",443],["+"," Viele von ihnen müssen allerdings erst gekocht werden: Rohe Bohnen, vor allem die Gartenbohne (Phaseolus vulgaris), deren älteste Funde um 6000 v. Chr. aus der Guitarrero-Höhle in Peru stammen, enthalten den Giftstoff Phasin (Phytohämagglutinin), ein Lektin, das rote Blutkörperchen verklumpt und heftige Magen-Darm-Beschwerden auslöst und erst durch gründliches Kochen zerstört wird."],["=",564]]}]},
